// Pull request: #6443 Detection vstest susp location
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6443
// Pull request author: Diablo-research
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Proxy Execution Via VSTest From Suspicious Location
// Sigma ID: 388d9887-45c5-43ad-a643-306c715eb385
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Nazar Diachok (@Diablo-research)
// Date: 2026-10-07 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects Microsoft VSTest Console executing a test assembly from a potentially suspicious user-
//   writable directory. Adversaries may abuse VSTest to execute code embedded in a crafted test
//   assembly.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate software testing or CI workflows that execute test assemblies from temporary or other user-writable directories.
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/test/vstest-console-options
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Vstest.console/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/73a0eb14c0dba4575fc1e58a5f0697164a6d917f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_vstest_susp_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\vstest.console.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "vstest.console.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\Temp\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\Windows\\Temp\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Users\\Public\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Downloads\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Desktop\\") and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe")
